 #edb/ref 17592186094940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094939 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "96962338-e491-50f7-b8da-1efc8b69ba83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094940 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094940 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094940 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae96c78f-e10d-563b-82af-e2c02160928e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094941 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{q + r}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094941 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094941 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "25f7a90e-939a-568d-ba3d-07a616fcb021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094942 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}} + \\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094942 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094942 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "328e6ad2-ef2f-5827-8881-60cdfaebb76b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094943 #edb/ref 1080 "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094943 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094943 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094944 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{q + r}{\\sqrt{13}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094944 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094944 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "703e463a-8826-5adf-9d3d-36bfd8037d83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096447 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096447 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $3$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096447 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2a61b115-4e26-5966-b2a9-d2fedef6b728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096447 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096448 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096448 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $10$, while the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $20$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a+b}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096448 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23d9a601-974b-51c2-a6ea-0ebadde19efc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096448 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $\\mathbf{a+b}$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ goes from the tail of $\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n![](images/32/32c48d8c19fc68fbc172b240ded922f3e2ebc12804411c318ff63fe999aaedcc.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $\\mathbf{a+b}$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + b & ^{2} &= & a & ^{2} +\\left.\\end{vmatrix}b\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&= 10^{2} + 20^{2} \\\\\n&= 100 + 400 \\\\\n&= 500\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a+b} &= \\sqrt{500}=10\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10\\sqrt{5}}(a + b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096493 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096493 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d3/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096493 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6dfe09f0-30e2-53bc-a8f6-d7e4a3b8232a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096493 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/b3/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{\\mid a \\mid} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186096969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502222 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502223 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502225 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502232 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502236 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502240 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502241 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502242 #edb/ref 17592