n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{49}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{29}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502397 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502426 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502397 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502397 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/02/02112c027add54e9bc7412151f3bd04c31d33e51eb1f96aded05b59e2489950e.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502397 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "baa6d129-80bc-5fdf-803e-edf7f11daa38" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502397 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d4/d4f6e1f602a4bf57830c11f0814f2fb7d6d1c2304421a32284f6bfb5a92690b5.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=1.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(\\frac{3}{2})^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{73}}{73}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502398 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502365 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502398 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502398 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b2/b25f39d9bbd30e928d8e07defbed4b2c3e3c4ef46ed92186fb83372dac14b1fd.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502398 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bbfa9f4f-6b90-5698-8173-56c2da86ba47" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [175