} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4+25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $\\sqrt{29}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{29}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502413 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502354 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502413 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502413 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b5/b58a1e76ec7f661d263be05a4e17826c99b1bce49e68ec5965c9ae91c4222e3c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d96e0a57-cd20-5e72-a2bf-50c93b37c3fb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502413 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/c6/c6d8bb8e64840dc44a7cd8e8fcab4c415147038f43eb12ad5186de620d8499b3.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(2)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+4} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $2 \\sqrt{5}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{10}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502417 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502362 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502417 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502417 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/27/27a852815532c69325ee58633141af9b34215fdb4e53058c8fa0fc3f73e74d37.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502417 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ddfae147-ff33-5d95-aa67-5f711e17eded" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502417 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/f1/f1880e8d87ec11f1199b3283f5eb4dfa32d4794bfc1