a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502430 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04e0f50e-8727-5a0b-b942-238de6b8a77f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502430 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=6^2+8^2\\\\\n&=36+64\\\\\n&=100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{100}=10\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{10}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502517 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502436 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502436 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $\\mid a|= 10$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-east and $\\mid b|= 15$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502436 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15e10e67-a13a-5e2d-88ee-bd7863909bbd" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502436 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=10^2+15^2\\\\\n&=100+225\\\\\n&=325\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{325}=5 \\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n